+
+## Check the mounting revision
+
+Drawing **BM-64 revision A** requires two external mounting ears and through holes at X = ±32.00 mm, Y = 0.00 mm. The design's build script reads back the base STEP and refuses a mismatched interface before it can publish a handoff. The same check runs during the delivered rebuild. To independently inspect both the installed base and its individual STEP export with the prepared CAD runtime, run:
+
+```sh
+"$PE_RUNTIME/bin/python" source/design/geometry/validation/verify_mounts.py . --report /tmp/bench-mount-readback.json
+```
+
+Require this check and the plugin assembly verification to pass before releasing a build. Fit the bench plate and choose two BM01 fasteners for its actual threaded depth. The original board and removable lid keep their mounting pattern and available clearance.
